        "runId": "ada-en-20261107-mw6m8vuu",
        "model": "GPT-6"
      },
      "text": "Today you will visit the archaeological site of Chichén Itzá, a UNESCO World Heritage Site. This large complex on the Yucatán Peninsula was an important regional centre of Maya civilisation and later came under Toltec influence. The city's architecture reflects this mix of styles.\n\nMany stone structures survive at the site, and some have been restored. The Pyramid of Kukulcán, also known as the Temple of Kukulcán, dominates the complex.\n\nAfter touring the site in the heat, continue to Ik Kil Cenote, where you can swim in the cool water of this natural limestone sinkhole.\n\nThen transfer to a hotel in Cancún or on the Riviera Maya. You can extend your beach stay or head to the international airport."
    },
